@title Cabinet: a device dragged near its rail clips onto it by its centre, one dragged away leaves it
@area Cabinet
@sizes 1366x768
# The cabinet lesson project after Place all: -K1 (85 mm high) sits on rail 92 with the rail line through its
# middle (top at y 210). A drag along the rail, a few millimetres off the line, lands back on the line and
# stays mounted; a drag well clear of every rail leaves the rail. Pictures: devices drawn with their typical
# fronts (screws, poles, vents), rails behind them.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-lesson.novo
wait 30
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 30
shot plate
check_blank plate
check_layout
click 624 329
wait 10
expect "55, 210 mm"
click 1100 399
wait 10
expect "Mounted on"
shot k1-selected
drag 624 329 640 334
wait 20
expect "210 mm"
expect_not "55, 210 mm"
expect "Mounted on"
shot k1-slid
drag 640 334 800 436
wait 20
expect_not "Mounted on"
shot k1-off-the-rail
check_layout
